course: dictionary
lesson: 913
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, look at the words and sentences around it. This is its context. «Blender and food processor blades can cut deep into fingers in a split second.» Here the clues are blender, food processor and cut, so blade must mean the sharp cutting part.
explain: Now try a different sentence: «Suleiman whispers: "Little man, you know that all your stamping wouldn't bend one blade of grass."» There is no knife or fan here. A blade of grass is one long, thin leaf of grass, and that is the meaning that fits.
explain: Ask yourself: what is being talked about? A knife, a fan, a grass leaf, a skate? Once you know the thing, you know which meaning of blade to use. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A blade is the flat, sharp cutting part of a knife, scissors, a saw or a sword.
fact: A blade of grass is one long, thin leaf of grass.
fact: A blade is also a flat part that spins or pushes, like on a fan, a propeller or an oar.
fact: The blade of an ice skate is the thin metal strip you glide on.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one. Look at the words around it first.
exercise: «Little man, you know that all your stamping wouldn't bend one blade of grass.» What is a blade here? | A sword | *One long, thin leaf of grass | A flat part that spins | A piece of metal for cutting
exercise: «Blender and food processor blades can cut deep into fingers in a split second.» What does blade mean here? | A single leaf | A thin strip you glide on | A bone in the shoulder | *A flat, sharp cutting part
exercise: Dad says, «Keep fan blades away from your fingers.» What do the fan blades do? | Cut the grass | Hold the fan up | *Spin round and push the air | Glide across ice
test: In a story, a knight draws his blade. What is his blade? | A leaf of grass | *A sword | A skate | A fan
test: «If a little child grabs something sharp, do not snatch it by the blade.» Why must you be careful with the blade of a knife? | Because knives are very heavy | Because blades are soft and bend | Because it is rude to touch knives | *Because the sharp part can cut you
exam: «At the vet's, a microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin between a puppy's shoulder blades.» What is a shoulder blade? | A sharp cutting part of a knife | *A bone in the back of the shoulder | A thin strip on an ice skate | A long, thin leaf
